# Paystack Integration Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the steps to integrate Paystack into the ticket registration flow for Benin Tech Fest. It will support both free registrations and paid ticket purchases.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> You will need to provide your Paystack API keys. We need to add the **Paystack Public Key** to your environment variables (`.env.local`) to initialize the payment popup on the frontend, and optionally the **Paystack Secret Key** if we want to verify payments on the server side.
> 
> Can you confirm if you already have a Paystack account and your API keys ready?

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> Currently, the backend registration route (`/api/submissions/registration`) saves data to a database. Should we also add a backend verification step to confirm the Paystack transaction using the Secret Key before saving the registration, or is relying on the frontend success callback sufficient for now?

## Proposed Changes

---

### Frontend Components

#### [MODIFY] [Registration.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/benin-tech-fest/app/components/Registration.tsx)
- Use `useSearchParams` from `next/navigation` to read the `tier` parameter from the URL.
- Display the selected ticket tier and its price above the form.
- Integrate `react-paystack` or the `@paystack/inline-js` script.
- Modify the form submission logic:
  - If the selected tier is **Free** (e.g., Community Pass), submit the form directly.
  - If the selected tier is **Paid**, trigger the Paystack payment popup.
  - After a successful Paystack payment, submit the registration data along with the payment reference to the backend.

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] `/api/submissions/registration` (Route Handler)
- Update the API route to accept a `paymentReference` or `tier` field.
- (Optional but recommended) Verify the payment reference with the Paystack API using the Secret Key before saving the registration to the database.

### Environment & Dependencies

#### [NEW] Dependencies
- Install `react-paystack` via `npm install react-paystack`.

#### [MODIFY] [.env.local](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/benin-tech-fest/.env.local)
- Add `NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=<your_public_key>`
- Add `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=<your_secret_key>` (for server-side verification)

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` to ensure no type errors or missing dependencies are introduced.

### Manual Verification
- Go to the Tickets section and select a Free tier, verify registration succeeds without payment.
- Select a Paid tier, fill out the form, verify the Paystack popup appears.
- Use Paystack test cards to complete a test payment.
- Verify that the success message is shown and the data is saved in the database.
